# tail.{{DOMAIN}} — tailnet entry point: the tailnet door list at / and the
# ttyd host shell at /ttyd.
#
# Access model — Tailscale MEMBERSHIP is the only gate, by operator choice:
#   * every path — non-tailnet sources get 403 (@not_tailnet)
#   * /            — the tailnet door list: every TAILNET-only route of this
#                    domain (the shell, one card per registered device
#                    session) fetched live from /targets.json on every visit.
#                    No login, no session, no commands.
#   * /targets.json — GENERATED catalogue (scripts/access/tail-targets.sh)
#   * /ttyd*      — the shell. Deliberately UNAUTHENTICATED: a tailnet device
#                    that can reach the vhost gets a root shell, no second
#                    credential (HTTP basic auth was removed 2026-09-22 by
#                    operator request — membership IS the auth). Reaching it
#                    non-tailnet is impossible: the 403 above runs first.
#
# Caching: NOTHING on this vhost may be cached — not the door list, not the
# catalogue, not ttyd responses. `no-store` (forbids storing), the ETag /
# Last-Modified deletes (no validators left to revalidate against) and the
# legacy Pragma/Expires headers make every request hit the edge fresh.
#
# TLS — two variants of the ONE tail door, chosen by the installer, never by
# hand. Normally tail.{{DOMAIN}} gets a Let's Encrypt cert (DNS-01, like every
# other vhost). But LE enforces a per-identifier rate limit (HTTP 429: 5 certs
# for an exact set of names per 168 h): when that one name is rate-limited,
# Caddy can never issue for it and the door answers 000 (TLS alert) instead of
# 403/200 — which is exactly the tail smoke failures of 2026-10-17. The
# installer then rolls THIS door only back to a cert minted by `tailscale cert`
# for the machine's own Tailscale HTTPS name, and serves the same door there.
# `TAIL_CERT_ROLLBACK` is written into instance.conf by the installer; no other
# vhost ever takes this branch.
{{IF TAIL_CERT_ROLLBACK}}
https://{{TS_CERT_HOST}} {
    # Emergency cert: static files minted by `tailscale cert` (written next to
    # the ACME store under /data), used until the LE limit lifts and a repair
    # run re-renders the normal block below.
    tls /data/tail-door.crt /data/tail-door.key
{{ELSE}}
https://tail.{{DOMAIN}} {
    tls {
        dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
    }
{{END}}
    import compress
    header {
        import security_headers
        # Nothing here may be cached: a stale cached response would keep
        # serving a state the next request would not confirm.
        Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0"
        Pragma "no-cache"
        Expires "0"
        -ETag
        -Last-Modified
    }
    route {
        @not_tailnet not remote_ip 100.64.0.0/10
        respond @not_tailnet 403

        # Generated navigation catalogue for the terminal.
        handle /targets.json {
            root * /srv/www
            file_server
        }

        # ttyd host terminal — no second credential (see the header). Base
        # path is /ttyd (ttyd -b /ttyd), so the full path is proxied as-is —
        # do not strip the prefix.
        handle /ttyd* {
            reverse_proxy 172.22.0.1:7681 {
                transport http {
                    versions 1.1
                }
            }
        }

        # The door list (static; modules/$DOMAIN/www is mounted read-only
        # at /srv/www in the caddy container).
        handle / {
            root * /srv/www
            rewrite /tail.html
            file_server
        }

        # Everything else is the plain "ok" stub.
        handle {
            respond "ok" 200
        }
    }
}
